                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 854.]</seg></opener>
                <head>THE EMPEROR’S NORTHERN JOURNEY.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[From the Tokei Times of <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-09-07">September 7,
                        1878</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>The northern journey of His Majesty the Emperor is marked by similar formal
                    ceremonies and jubilant popular demonstrations to those which distinguished his
                    progress last year.</p>
                <p>His Majesty visits the schools, public offices, and temples on his route, is
                    received with suitable honors, and usually leaves tokens of remembrance behind
                    him. Thus far the Imperial party have had nothing but agreeable, though not
                    especially stirring, experiences to encounter.</p>
            </div>
